  - m_Id: 543263415525382
    m_Localized: Metabolic Acceleration Blood
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 543263415525383
    m_Localized: Metabolic Inhibitor Serum
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 543263415525384
    m_Localized: Modified Predator Claw
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 543263415525385
    m_Localized: Mutagenic Fluid Slime
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 543263415525386
    m_Localized: Pressure-Adaptive Scale Shard
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 543263415525387
    m_Localized: Regenerated Bone Marrow
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 543263415525388
    m_Localized: Reinforced Carapace
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 543263415525389
    m_Localized: Self-Regeneration Serum
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 543263415525390
    m_Localized: Volatile Gas Sac
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 544373287084032
    m_Localized: Complex Suppression Serum
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 901934343446528
    m_Localized: Extract from Monster Spine
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 752864434348032
    m_Localized: Victor's Diary
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 754063640387584
    m_Localized: Project Participant
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 754063640387585
    m_Localized: Subject Folder
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1078952628510720
    m_Localized: '*WARNING*


      OPEN ONLY

      FOR ESCAPE

      (ALARM WILL
      SOUND)'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1440805049262080
    m_Localized: "\u25CF Composition: Ultra-high-strength chitin variant\n\u25CF
      Effect: Increases muscle fiber density."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1440805166702592
    m_Localized: "\u25CF Composition: Metabolic acceleration enzyme\n\u25CF Effect:
      Accelerates cellular energy production. <b>Overuse may cause physical overload.</b>"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1440805166702593
    m_Localized: "\u25CF Composition: Pressure-adaptive minerals, Factor S1\n\u25CF
      Effect: <b>Enhances inter-tissue cohesion</b> to stabilize the body structure."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1440805166702594
    m_Localized: "\u25CF Composition: Low-temperature adaptive suppression factor\n\u25CF
      Effect: <b>Control and stabilization of chemical reaction rates.</b>"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1440805166702595
    m_Localized: "\u25CF Composition: Lattice-structured low-temperature adaptive
      mineral complex\n\u25CF Effect: Simultaneously grants high flexibility and
      extreme cold resistance to the exoskeleton. <b>Prevents cell membrane destruction
      during rapid temperature changes and high-pressure environments.</b>"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1440805166702596
    m_Localized: "\u25CF Composition: High-hardness bio-ceramic variant\n\u25CF Effect:
      Raw material for hardening agents and stability testing of tissue-strengthening
      drugs."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1440805166702597
    m_Localized: "\u25CF Composition: Cell mutation-promoting enzyme\n\u25CF Effect:
      Induces abnormal cell growth and morphological mutation."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1440805166702598
    m_Localized: "\u25CF Composition: Factor H2\n\u25CF Effect: Blocks specific intracellular
      signal transduction pathways to <b>forcibly slow down abnormal metabolic rates.</b>"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1440805166702599
    m_Localized: "\u25CF Composition: Highly volatile diffusion medium\n\u25CF Effect:
      Acts as a medium that instantly vaporizes and diffuses liquid compounds into
      the air.\n\u25CF <mark=#FF000044>Note: [DANGER]</mark> Upon sac rupture, contents
      instantly vaporize and spread within a 5m radius. Utilized as an essential
      ingredient for wide-area dispersal of special compounds."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1440805166702600
    m_Localized: "\u25CF Composition: Self-regeneration inducing serum\n\u25CF Effect:
      <b>Accelerates repair at the cellular level.</b>"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1440805166702601
    m_Localized: "\u25CF Composition: Immune cell amplification enzyme\n\u25CF Effect:
      Dramatic activation of biological immune response."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1440805166702602
    m_Localized: "\u25CF Composition: Highly concentrated immune-promoting protein
      Factor H1\n\u25CF Effect: <b>Grants resistance against strong light and radiation.</b>"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1440805166702603
    m_Localized: "\u25CF Composition: Hematopoietic and osteogenic inducing cells\n\u25CF
      Effect: Induces osteoblasts within the marrow and <b>promotes skeletal regeneration.</b>"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1440805166702604
    m_Localized: "\u25CF Composition: Immune stabilizing factor\n\u25CF Effect: Alleviates
      hyper-active immune responses. (<b>Maintains biological balance</b> when mixed
      with octopus components)"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1440805166702605
    m_Localized: "\u25CF Composition: Calcium-pressure adaptive protein\n\u25CF Effect:
      Enhances bone density and external skeletal strength."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1440805166702606
    m_Localized: "\n<b>Overview</b>\nBio-response analysis of immune-promoting proteins
      extracted from the photophore tissue of the Abyssal Immune Octopus.\n\n<b>[
      Subject ]</b>\nSpecimen Code: AI-OCT-04\nExtraction Site: Photophore\nExtracted
      Component: <color=#FFCC00><b>Factor H1</b></color>\n\n<b>[ Observation Data
      ]</b>\nFactor H1 exhibits an extremely high bio-active response, and has been
      confirmed to maintain the specimen's tissue stability under photon stimulation
      environments.\nUpon administration to the test subject, nervous system hypersensitivity
      was significantly reduced even under strong illumination and radiation exposure.\nIn
      particular, the abnormal light sensitivity induced by <color=#FFCC00><b>Factor
      X1</b></color> was mostly eliminated.\n\n<b>[ Analysis Results ]</b>\n<color=#FFCC00><b>Factor
      H1 is determined to directly suppress the activation mechanism of Factor X1.</b></color>\nFollowing
      administration, the following symptoms were stabilized:\n\u25CF Muscle tissue
      hyper-proliferation\n\u25CF Light source avoidance response\n\u25CF Optic nerve
      stimulation surge\nThis component demonstrates the highest stability among
      X1 inhibitors identified to date."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1440805166702607
    m_Localized: '#01-AI Immune Response Analysis'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1440805166702608
    m_Localized: '#02-BL Metabolic Inhibition Analysis'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1440805166702609
    m_Localized: "<b>Overview</b>\nBio-metabolic inhibition property and Factor X2
      reactivity analysis of Factor H2, an extracted component from the Blackriver
      Leech.\n\n<b>[ Subject ]</b>\nSpecimen Code: BR-LCH-02\nExtraction Site: Metabolic
      Inhibitor Serum\nExtracted Component: <color=#FFCC00><b>Factor H2</b></color>\n\n<b>[
      Observation Data ]</b>\nFactor H2 exhibited properties of forcibly blocking
      specific intracellular signal transduction pathways to reduce abnormal cellular
      activation rates.\nIn single-administration experiments, the inhibition effect
      on Factor X2 activation was incomplete, and the subject's aggressiveness as
      well as tissue mutation speed did not significantly decrease.\nHowever, when
      combined with <color=#FFCC00><b>Factor S1</b></color>, an extracted component
      from the Abyssal Predator Crab, to form a complex, a rapid decline in <color=#FFCC00><b>Factor
      X2</b></color> activation reactivity was observed.\n\n<b>[ Analysis Results
      ]</b>\nFollowing <color=#FFCC00><b>Factor H2-S1 complex administration</b></color>,
      the following symptoms were stabilized:\n\u25CF Increased aggressive impulse\n\u25CF
      Auditory hypersensitivity\n\u25CF Nervous system surge\nDemonstrated the highest
      <b>Factor X2</b> inhibition efficiency among substances identified to date.\n\n<b>[
      Side Effects & Notes ]</b>\nSevere psychiatric symptoms were reported in test
      subjects following complex administration.\nPrimary cases:\n\u25CF <color=#FF4444><b>Hallucinations</b></color>\n\u25CF
      <color=#FF4444><b>Extreme increase in aggressiveness</b></color>\nSome test
      subjects exhibit behavior of repeatedly striking containment walls.\nThe cause
      of side effects is currently under investigation."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1440805166702610
    m_Localized: '#03-SC Crystallization Reaction Analysis'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1440805183479808
    m_Localized: "\n<b>Overview</b>\nThermodynamic reaction analysis on epidermal
      tissue and crystallized scale samples of the Crystal-Scale Dragonfish.\n\n<b>[
      Subject ]</b>\nSpecimen Code: SC-DFS-03\nExtraction Site: Crystallized Scale\nPrimary
      Component: <color=#FFCC00><b>Low-Temperature Adaptive Mineral Complex</b></color>\n\n<b>[
      Observation Data ]</b>\nThe integumentary scales of this specimen were confirmed
      to maintain a stable crystal lattice structure even in extreme cold and high-pressure
      environments below 5,000m deep sea.\nThe crystal layer disperses external pressure
      while suppressing cell membrane damage, maintaining tissue stability even in
      environments with rapid temperature changes.\nHowever, when thermal energy
      above a certain threshold is applied externally, the internal mineral bonds
      of the crystal collapse, causing the surface structure to undergo <color=#FFCC00><b>recrystallization</b></color>.\nDuring
      this process, highly concentrated mineral residues separate from the crystal
      layer.\n\n<b>[ Analysis Results ]</b>\nThe separated crystal components exhibited
      strong reaction stabilization properties,\n<color=#FFCC00><b>and were confirmed
      to act as a neutralizing agent during the H2-S1 complex formulation process.</b></color>\nFollowing
      administration, the following symptoms were temporarily alleviated:\n\u25CF
      Neural hypersensitivity\n\u25CF Hallucinations\n\u25CF Auditory overload\n\u25CF
      Cellular activity imbalance\nIn particular, the acute nervous system rejection
      reaction occurring immediately after complex administration was significantly
      reduced, and the specimen's neural waveforms approached stable levels.\n\n<b>[
      Risk Factors & Warnings ]</b>\n<color=#FF4444><b>If the critical temperature
      is exceeded during the crystal separation process,</b></color>\na phenomenon
      where components rapidly degenerate and evaporate was observed.\nByproducts
      generated after degeneration exhibit <color=#FF4444><b>strong neuro-irritant
      properties</b></color>, with the following symptoms reported:\n\u25CF Muscle
      tissue hyper-proliferation\n\u25CF Auditory hallucinations\n\u25CF Visual distortion\n<color=#00FFFF><b>In
      the absence of heating equipment, an alternative extraction method utilizing
      friction heat from high-speed rotation devices is recommended.</b></color>\nHowever,
      upon extraction failure, there is a risk of high-temperature debris release
      alongside crystal layer collapse."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1440805183479809
    m_Localized: '#09-CH Blue Binding Structure'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1440805183479810
    m_Localized: '

      <b>[ Observation Data ]</b>

      Following the mixture
      of specific samples, a phenomenon where <color=#FFCC00><b>vivid blue crystals
      connected in hexagonal chain forms</b></color> was observed within the microscopic
      field of view.

      The structure remains stable for a certain period, exhibiting
      properties that reduce the reaction rate around cellular tissue.


      <b>[
      Additional Reactions ]</b>

      In some samples, a phenomenon where <color=#FFCC00><b>red
      cellular tissue attached around the crystal chains</b></color> was confirmed.

      Structures
      bound with red cells had a relatively slower collapse speed, and tissue discoloration
      reactions were also reduced.

      Conversely, structures lacking red cells
      began to crack rapidly after a certain period.


      <b>[ Contamination Reaction
      ]</b>

      In incomplete samples, a <color=#FFCC00><b>black fragment structure</b></color>
      was observed.

      Following the occurrence of the contamination reaction,
      the blue crystal structure collapsed rapidly, and some samples degenerated
      into a black color.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1440805183479811
    m_Localized: '#01 Metastasis Phase Tracking Log'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1440805183479812
    m_Localized: "\n<b>Overview</b>\nObservation log of body temperature changes
      and behavioral pattern transition processes in test subjects infected with
      X-series mutation factors.\n\n<b>[ Phase-by-Phase Observation Log ]</b>\n<size=80%><color=#AAAAAA><pos=7%>Observed
      Symptoms & Behavioral Signs<pos=52%>Measured Temp<pos=77%>Log Date</color></size>\n------------------------------------------------------------\n
      No unusual findings. Subject normal.<pos=55%>37\xB0C<pos=75%>2004-03-01\n Extreme
      pain response to lights.<pos=55%>38\xB0C<pos=75%>2004-03-03\n Hypersensitive
      response to high-frequency noise.<pos=55%>40\xB0C<pos=75%>2004-03-06\n Exoskeleton
      can be freely adjusted.<pos=55%>42\xB0C<pos=75%>2004-03-10\n <color=#FF4444>Measurement
      Impossible (ERROR)</color><pos=55%><color=#FF4444>44\xB0C</color><pos=75%>2004-03-17\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\n<b>[
      Special Notes ]</b>\nA phenomenon was confirmed where aggressiveness, sensory
      hypersensitivity, and skeletal deformity speeds increased proportionally with
      body temperature elevation.\nAfter 42\xB0C, the subject repeatedly attacked
      the walls continuously without external stimuli, and the internal skeletal
      structure began to expand abnormally.\n\n<b>[ Emergency Log ]</b>  <size=80%><color=#AAAAAA>2004-03-17
      20:13:22</color></size>\n<color=#FF4444>Upon the test subject's body temperature
      reaching 43.8\xB0C, all measuring equipment inside the containment room overloaded.\nThe
      subject's spinal tissue began to protrude rapidly, and maintaining the existing
      humanoid skeletal structure was deemed impossible.\nEstimated time to reach
      44\xB0C is approximately 30 seconds.\nEvacuation order for all researchers
      is executed as of this moment.</color>"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1440805183479813
    m_Localized: '#02 Optical Stimulus Response'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1440805183479814
    m_Localized: '

      <b>Overview</b>

      Analysis of bio-responses and tissue
      changes occurring when mutant test subjects are exposed to light sources of
      specific wavelengths.


      <b>[ Subject ]</b>

      Equipment Used: High-Power
      Photon Irradiator

      Analysis Factor: <b>Factor X1</b>


      <b>[ Observation
      Data ]</b>

      When exposed to light of specific wavelengths, the test subject
      exhibited an immediate avoidance response.

      In the initial stage, it
      was merely at the level of simple spasms, but as exposure time increased, exoskeleton
      surface cracking and tissue collapse phenomena occurred.

      The exoskeleton
      on the subject''s back split abnormally, and internal tissue began to protrude.

      Subsequently,
      <color=#FF4444><b>new joint structures were formed on both sides of the spine</b></color>,
      and the newly formed tissue moved independently from the existing skeleton.


      <b>[
      Analysis Results ]</b>

      <color=#FF4444><b>Factor X1 remaining in the
      body is determined to react with external photon stimuli, overstimulating the
      nervous system.</b></color>

      In strong light-stimulation environments,
      cellular mutation speed increases rapidly, and an explosive progression of
      previously suppressed tissue reorganization was confirmed.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1440805183479815
    m_Localized: '#03 Acoustic Stimulus Response'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1440805183479816
    m_Localized: '

      <b>Overview</b>

      Analysis of nervous system and behavioral
      responses of mutant test subjects occurring in high-frequency acoustic stimulus
      environments.


      <b>[ Subject ]</b>

      Equipment Used: High-Frequency
      Generator

      Analysis Factor: <color=#FF4444><b>Factor X2</b></color>


      <b>[
      Observation Data ]</b>

      A rapid increase in the subject''s aggressiveness
      was confirmed upon the generation of high-frequency noise above a certain frequency.

      The
      subject exhibited repetitive charging behavior toward the acoustic generation
      device, and muscle rigidity as well as spinal reflex responses also rose abnormally.

      After
      approximately 40 to 60 seconds, the subject fell into a state of general paralysis.


      <b>[
      Analysis Results ]</b>

      <color=#FF4444><b>Factor X2 formed during the
      mutation process is determined to have abnormally enlarged the auditory organ
      receptors.</b></color>

      Neural excitation levels increase explosively
      within specific frequency bands.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1440805183479817
    m_Localized: ABYSSAL PREDATOR CRAB
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1440805183479818
    m_Localized: "\u25CF Giant crustaceans with abnormally developed exoskeletons.\n\u25CF
      They possess genes for extreme environmental adaptation, and the minerals inside
      their bodies react with specific factors to induce a <color=#FF8C00>powerful
      hardening reaction.</color>"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1440805183479819
    m_Localized: CRYSTAL SCALE DRAGONFISH
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1440805183479820
    m_Localized: "\u25CF A predatory deep-sea fish optimized for <b>extreme cold
      and high-pressure environments</b> at depths below 5,000m.\n\u25CF Contains
      complex suppression factors inside its body, inducing a <color=#00FFFF>neutralization
      reaction</color> when mixed with other substances."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1440805183479821
    m_Localized: BLACKRIVER LEECH
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1440805183479822
    m_Localized: "\u25CF An invertebrate that absorbs organic matter and replaces
      it with mutation-promoting slime.\n\u25CF Possesses a <color=#FF0000>diffusion
      ability via internal gas sacs</color>, and contains a large amount of Factor
      H2, the core mechanism of mutation."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1440805183479823
    m_Localized: ABYSSAL IMMUNE OCTOPUS
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1440805183479824
    m_Localized: "\u25CF An entity that evolved a <b>Hyper-active Immune System</b>
      to survive in extreme water pressure environments.\n\u25CF Specific enzymes
      within its tentacle mucus induce explosive proliferation of immune cells, resulting
      in abnormally fast tissue regeneration rates.\n\u25CF Uncontrolled <b><color=#FFCC00>cellular
      hyper-proliferation</color></b> phenomena reported in some test subjects."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1440805183479825
    m_Localized: REGENERATIVE MARROW SEAHORSE
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1440805183479826
    m_Localized: "\u25CF A unique seahorse species inhabiting areas near deep-sea
      hydrothermal vents.\n\u25CF Possesses highly active <b>marrow activity</b>,
      enabling immediate self-repair even upon skeletal amputation.\n\u25CF Contains
      stabilizing factors that <color=#00FF7F>soothe hyper-active immunity</color>."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1538993072562176
    m_Localized: Analysis of the Immune Response of <b>Abyssal Immune Octopus Photophore</b>
      Tissue
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
