    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1546705013497856
    m_Localized: Experiment Record
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1546705109966848
    m_Localized: Species List
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1546705109966849
    m_Localized: Biological Characteristics
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1546705109966850
    m_Localized: Sample
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1559942241116160
    m_Localized: 'Starting today, I am deployed to the <color=#C80000>deep-sea creature
      exploration mission</color>.


      Elena, Sophia, and Lucas saw me off at
      the pier, while Buddy and Charlie ran around happily. The kids smiled until
      the end, but Elena clearly tried to hide her worry.


      Right after reaching
      the sub, I organized my room. Inside my locker, I taped Sophia''s family drawing
      and photos of Buddy and Charlie. Seeing them will give me strength. Leaving
      family behind is never easy, but exploring and capturing unknown deep-sea life
      still excites me.


      The specimens we capture go to researchers, hopefully
      leading to new cures or technology that help people. It is dangerous, but worth
      it. I must finish safely and return home.


      My roommate is my subordinate,
      Aaron Dyer. He looked tense all through boarding. It is his first time seeing
      deep-sea life, and he seems too scared for capture duty, but experience will
      help him grow.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1559942371139584
    m_Localized: 'Today, I did our first patrol and equipment check.


      Researchers
      were busy all day analyzing new deep-sea specimens. To us, they are dangerous
      creatures, but to them, valuable data.


      I briefly chatted with Chloe
      Reynolds in the cafeteria. Once she starts talking research, she loses track
      of time.


      Aaron still gets super tense whenever he passes the lab.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1559942371139585
    m_Localized: 'Today was <color=#C80000>Commander Robert Hayes</color>''s birthday.


      He
      is usually strict enough not to overlook even small mistakes, but he showed
      a rare smile at the small celebration we prepared. The mood in the submarine
      brightened up for the first time in a while.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1559942371139586
    m_Localized: 'Today, I went outside the submarine on a deep-sea exploration mission.


      Whenever
      I enter the <color=#C80000>escape room</color>, I feel nervous. When I <color=#C80000>close
      the internal hatch</color> and the seawater slowly rises, I feel suffocated.
      When I first took on this task, I broke out in a cold sweat just because the
      water rose to my throat.


      What''s really important, however, is next.
      When the external seawater is full, the government should not rush and <color=#C80000>adjust
      the pressure</color> first. In the deep sea, water pressure instantly weighs
      on the body, and if this process is skipped, ear-wrenching pain can occur.


      I
      always cover my nose and push my breath slowly to apply pressure to the inside
      of my ears before going outside. The trick is to repeat it over and over again
      until you feel okay. I''ve seen several new recruits who are struggling while
      trying to leave in a hurry.


      Even today, Aaron was so nervous that he
      couldn''t balance the pressure properly that he grabbed his ear and frowned
      for a long time. I''ve told him over and over again, but in the deep sea, following
      the procedure is more about saving your life than rushing.


      The expedition
      was completed successfully, and a deep-sea creature that had never been seen
      before was also secured. There are risks, but the moment you directly discover
      a creature that has not yet been known to the world, your heart always throbs.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1559942371139587
    m_Localized: "After shift, I worked out for the first time in a while. Capture
      duty takes a lot of stamina, so keeping fit is a must.\n\nIn the evening, I
      played cards with the crew. Aaron just watched awkwardly at first, but eventually
      joined in\u2014turns out he's pretty competitive, which got everyone laughing.\n\nIt
      made a tiring day feel a bit lighter."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1559942371139588
    m_Localized: "Today\u2019s exploration went smoothly as well.\n\nChloe explained
      her new findings with an excited look while studying the deep-sea creature
      we caught a few days ago. She succeeded in extracting a serum that induces
      self-regeneration. Though it's still in the research phase, she was thrilled,
      saying it could save many lives one day.\n\nListening to her, I felt like I
      understood a bit more why we risk coming down into the deep sea."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1559942371139589
    m_Localized: 'Tomorrow is <color=#C80000>Officer Daniel Boyd</color>''s birthday.


      Since
      he always puts the crew first, everyone is preparing small gifts. In a confined
      space like this, even a minor event brightens the mood quite a bit.


      Seeing
      Aaron seriously ponder what to get for the officer, it seems he has adapted
      to some extent. His expression looks more relaxed than when he first boarded.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1559942371139590
    m_Localized: 'Today will probably be a day I will never forget.


      One of
      the deep-sea creatures being studied suddenly broke through containment and
      escaped. As soon as the alarm went off, I led the security team and rushed
      to the scene.


      The thing went wild, firing <color=#C80000>sharp spines</color>
      from its back in all directions. We managed to subdue it, but my fingertips
      are still trembling from the tension.


      What haunts me most is its appearance.
      Its body structure and movement were eerily similar to a <color=#C80000>human</color>.
      A chill ran down my spine the moment our eyes met. It felt far too grotesque
      to be a simple deep-sea creature.


      I don''t think I''ll be able to fall
      asleep easily tonight.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1782114578522112
    m_Localized: Reunion with a Familiar Nightmare
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1782114687574016
    m_Localized: 'It was "something" that used to be a comrade.

      Spider-like
      legs sprouting from its back scraped against the metal corridor, approaching
      at a grotesque speed.

      .....Your final scream scattered among torn flesh.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1782114687574017
    m_Localized: The Deep Sea's Period
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1782114687574018
    m_Localized: 'The submarine shook violently under immense water pressure.

      A
      explosion followed.

      The monster of the deep sea found you at last.

      .....And
      nothing remained.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1782114687574019
    m_Localized: To the Lowest Place
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1782114687574020
    m_Localized: 'Gravity dragged you down into a deeper abyss.

      After a brief
      scream, only a dull rupture echoed.

      .....The cold submarine floor became
      your final bed.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1782114687574021
    m_Localized: The Price of Arrogant Certainty
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1782114687574022
    m_Localized: "To think you couldn't solve even a simple puzzle like this.\nSelf-destructing
      before being eaten by the monster\u2014\nIs there a more ridiculous end than
      this?\n.....Not even death could mask your stupidity."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1782114687574023
    m_Localized: Passing Down the Nightmare
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1782114687574024
    m_Localized: 'A brain-melting fever took over your entire body.

      Spines
      slowly sprouting through the skin on your back finally grew full-grown into
      massive deadly weapons with bone-crushing pain.

      Where the human body
      collapsed, a perfect monster now stands tall.

      The reason of "you," once
      human, withered into the cold deep sea forever.

      .....Now it is your
      turn to become someone''s familiar nightmare.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1782114687574025
    m_Localized: Eyes of a Greater Abyss
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1782114687574026
    m_Localized: "You barely made it to the escape pod.\nOnly now do you let out
      a sigh of relief.\nBut only for a moment\u2014a massive \"something\" is approaching
      outside the submarine.\n.....Did you truly reach \"escape\"?"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
